  "raw": {
    "https://farmingdale.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204975": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Horticulture",
      "description": "Farmingdale State College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Horticulture Farmingdale State College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Horticulture Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor - Horticulture Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Urban Horticulture & Design Locations: Farmingdale, NY Posted: Sep 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 27-01 Position ID: 204975 Share About Farmingdale State College: Farmingdale State College (FSC), the largest college of applied science and technology within the State University of New York system, is recognized for its applied learning. It enrolls over 10,000 students and offers nearly 50 degree programs through four schools: Arts and Sciences, Business, the Pasternack School of Engineering Technology, and the Santmann School of Health Sciences. The college's diverse offerings include the region's largest collegiate flight school, the only four-year dental hygiene program in the area, a nursing program with a 100% NCLEX pass rate, and a graduate portfolio aligned with regional needs. Master's degrees include construction management, nursing administration, and quality assurance and regulatory affairs, with additional programs in development. This is a college on the move. Construction is underway on a $75 million, 52,000-square-foot Computer Sciences Center, the first zero-net-carbon-ready building on campus, designed for our growing computing programs. Our corporate partners, including PSEG Long Island and Estée Lauder, provide scholarship funds, training programs, internships, and insight into the skills our students need to succeed.  The college's regional economic impact in 2025 was $272 million, according to an analysis conducted by the LIA Research. Faculty at FSC combine excellent teaching with active scholarship that involves undergraduates. The College has one of the most diverse student populations in the SUNY system and is federally recognized as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution. In 2026, FSC received the Higher Education Excellence and Distinction (HEED) Award from INSIGHT Into Academia. It ranks in the top 1% of colleges nationwide on the Social Mobility Index. We invite candidates from all backgrounds who are energized by the mission of public higher education and by the students it serves. Our 380-acre campus sits in the center of Long Island, roughly 35 miles from New York City, surrounded by a dense corridor of aerospace, health care, and technology employers, with beaches and parkland minutes away. Students connect through NCAA Division III athletics and an extensive array of clubs and organizations, and FSC has a strong culture of civic responsibility. If you want your teaching and scholarship to impact students' careers and a region's economy, FSC is the place. Job Description: The Department of Urban Horticulture and Design at Farmingdale State College invites applications for a full-time (10-month), tenure-track Assistant Professor of Horticulture position.  The successful candidate will teach courses within the department's recently revised Bachelor of Science program in Urban Horticulture. The Urban Horticulture B.S. program prepares students for contemporary careers in sustainable horticulture and urban environmental management through an emphasis on sustainable horticultural practices, native plants, permaculture, urban ecology, sustainable turfgrass management, and small-scale food production. We seek an individual who is prepared and able to teach both core courses, including introductory horticulture, plant materials, and diseases and pests, as well as specialized elective courses that reflect emerging trends and professional practices.  These courses will equip graduates with applied skills for careers in one or more of the following areas: sustainable horticulture, plant health care, urban greening, small-scale food production, and commercial and residential turfgrass management. All faculty members at Farmingdale State College have three workload components: teaching, research and scholarly activity, and service.  Candidates should have a research agenda that complements their area of academic specialty resulting in peer-reviewed publications, which are necessary for promotion and tenure at Farmingdale State College.  We are also interested in candidates with a history of, or interest in, pursuing external funding for their research.  The successful candidate will demonstrate an interest and high level of competence in teaching.  The service component of the workload includes student advising and participation on committees. The successful candidate will teach 12 contact hours per semester, including day and evening classes that may also include online and hybrid formats. The college particularly welcomes candidates with knowledge, skills and abilities that include: Commitment to diversity and university initiatives supportive of diversity and inclusion. Interest in participating in student-centered service activities. Desire to apply expertise in promoting civic engagement with the College's many community partners. Requirements: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. in Horticulture or a closely related field (such as plant science, plant biology, agricultural sciences) from a regionally accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered, provided the doctorate is conferred by the time of appointment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Previous college teaching or post-doc experience in a lab or research setting. Established research program as demonstrated by conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications, or other scholarly activities. Additional Information: This is a 10-month UUP faculty position. For the first 10 working days, beginning Friday, September 18, 2026 , and ending Thursday, October 1, 2026 , applications will be limited to UUP Farmingdale. CLOSING DATE FOR RECEIPT OF APPLICATIONS: Open Until Filled, with priority consideration given to applications received by Saturday, October 17, 2026. SALARY: $75,000 + $4,150 in downstate location pay = $79,150 Total Compensation. Salary may increase commensurate with qualifications and experience. ANTICIPATED START DATE: Fall semester 2027 The State University of New York offers excellent fringe benefits including health insurance options and retirement plans. Click here for New York State Benefits Summary Visit our Why Work at FSC page to learn more about FSC and the total rewards we offer. The Consumer Information web page can be viewed at the following link http://www.farmingdale.edu/consumer-information/index.shtml This page describes various services, information and statistics on many different aspects of the College's operations. Farmingdale State College's commitment to inclusive excellence is an important part of our mission of public education and our culture. At Farmingdale State College, we continue to work on building a community that supports freedom, mutual respect, and civility. We seek others who support these values of diversity and inclusiveness and candidates of all diverse backgrounds who wish to participate in our cultural aspirations are welcome and encouraged to apply. The College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status or any other legally protected status. Application Instructions: Interested candidates may apply by clicking on the \"Apply Now\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The following documents are required for all positions: Cover Letter Resume/C.V. Additional instructions for faculty positions: Your cover letter must include a statement on teaching philosophy and methodology. Please attach copies of teaching evaluations. Candidates invited for interviews will be asked to make a presentation on their research/creative activities as well as a separate teaching demonstration. Only applications made through Farmingdale's electronic application system will be accepted. Once you successfully apply you will receive an email as confirmation. Returning applicants may login to their Farmingdale State College Careers Account to apply for this position. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2350 Broadhollow Road Farmingdale, NY 11735-1021"
    },
    "https://farmingdale.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205562": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Nursing",
      "description": "Farmingdale State College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Nursing Farmingdale State College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Nursing Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor - Nursing Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Farmingdale, NY Posted: Oct 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 27-02 Position ID: 205562 Share About Farmingdale State College: Farmingdale State College (FSC), the largest college of applied science and technology within the State University of New York system, is recognized for its applied learning. It enrolls over 10,000 students and offers nearly 50 degree programs through four schools: Arts and Sciences, Business, the Pasternack School of Engineering Technology, and the Santmann School of Health Sciences. The college's diverse offerings include the region's largest collegiate flight school, the only four-year dental hygiene program in the area, a nursing program with a 100% NCLEX pass rate, and a graduate portfolio aligned with regional needs. Master's degrees include construction management, nursing administration, and quality assurance and regulatory affairs, with additional programs in development. This is a college on the move. Construction is underway on a $75 million, 52,000-square-foot Computer Sciences Center, the first zero-net-carbon-ready building on campus, designed for our growing computing programs. Our corporate partners, including PSEG Long Island and Estée Lauder, provide scholarship funds, training programs, internships, and insight into the skills our students need to succeed.  The college's regional economic impact in 2025 was $272 million, according to an analysis conducted by the LIA Research. Faculty at FSC combine excellent teaching with active scholarship that involves undergraduates. The College has one of the most diverse student populations in the SUNY system and is federally recognized as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution. In 2026, FSC received the Higher Education Excellence and Distinction (HEED) Award from INSIGHT Into Academia. It ranks in the top 1% of colleges nationwide on the Social Mobility Index. We invite candidates from all backgrounds who are energized by the mission of public higher education and by the students it serves. Our 380-acre campus sits in the center of Long Island, roughly 35 miles from New York City, surrounded by a dense corridor of aerospace, health care, and technology employers, with beaches and parkland minutes away. Students connect through NCAA Division III athletics and an extensive array of clubs and organizations, and FSC has a strong culture of civic responsibility. If you want your teaching and scholarship to impact students' careers and a region's economy, FSC is the place. Job Description: The Department of Nursing at Farmingdale State College invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Nursing. We seek a dynamic, student-focused educator who is committed to teaching excellence in teaching, scholarly engagement, and service to both the College and broader community. The successful candidate will support the academic mission of the Department of Nursing through teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate programs, contributing to curriculum development and assessment, engaging in scholarly activities, and participating in departmental and institutional service. All faculty members at Farmingdale State College have three workload components: teaching, research and scholarly activity, and service.  Candidates should have a research agenda that complements their area of academic specialty resulting in peer-reviewed publications, which are necessary for promotion and tenure at Farmingdale State College.  We are also interested in candidates with a history of, or interest in, pursuing external funding for their research.  The successful candidate will demonstrate an interest and high level of competence in teaching.  The service component of the workload includes student advising and participation on committees. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate nursing courses in classroom, clinical, simulation, and/or online learning environments. Provide academic advising, support, and mentorship to nursing students. Actively participate in curriculum development, assessment, and continuous program improvement initiatives in alignment with accreditation standards (e.g., CCNE, AACN Essentials). Engage in scholarly and professional development activities, including research, presentations, or publications. Collaborate with colleagues to promote student success through innovative, evidence-based teaching and learning strategies. Contribute to departmental, college-wide, and community service initiatives, including committee participation and related activities. Maintain current clinical expertise and professional knowledge within the assigned teaching area(s). Teaching assignments may include both day and evening classes, as well as possible online and/or hybrid course engagement. A Doctorate in Nursing or a related field is required to be considered for tenure. The college particularly welcomes candidates with knowledge, skills and abilities that include: Commitment to diversity and university initiatives supportive of diversity and inclusion. Interest in participating in student-centered service activities. Desire to apply expertise in promoting civic engagement with the College's many community partners. Requirements: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master's degree in Nursing. Unencumbered RN license in NY or eligible for licensure. Recent clinical experience in a healthcare setting. Evidence of strong communication, organizational, and technology skills. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Nursing or related discipline. Experience with simulation and innovative instructional technologies. Record of scholarship, publication, or professional presentations. Previous teaching experience in higher education. Additional Information: This is a 10-month UUP faculty position. For the first 10 working days, beginning Tuesday, October 6, 2026 , and ending Monday, October 19, 2026 , applications will be limited to UUP Farmingdale. CLOSING DATE FOR RECEIPT OF APPLICATIONS: Open Until Filled, with priority consideration given to applications received by Wednesday, November 4, 2026. SALARY: Competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ANTICIPATED START DATE: Fall semester 2026 The State University of New York offers excellent fringe benefits including health insurance options and retirement plans. Click here for New York State FT UUP Benefits Summary Visit our Why Work at FSC page to learn more about FSC and the total rewards we offer. The Consumer Information web page can be viewed at the following link http://www.farmingdale.edu/consumer-information/index.shtml This page describes various services, information and statistics on many different aspects of the College's operations. Farmingdale State College's commitment to inclusive excellence is an important part of our mission of public education and our culture. At Farmingdale State College, we continue to work on building a community that supports freedom, mutual respect, and civility. We seek others who support these values of diversity and inclusiveness and candidates of all diverse backgrounds who wish to participate in our cultural aspirations are welcome and encouraged to apply. The College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status or any other legally protected status. Application Instructions: Interested candidates may apply by clicking on the \"Apply Now\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The following documents are required for all positions: Cover Letter Resume/C.V. Additional instructions for faculty positions: Your cover letter must include a statement on teaching philosophy and methodology. Please attach copies of teaching evaluations. Candidates invited for interviews will be asked to make a presentation on their research/creative activities as well as a separate teaching demonstration. Only applications made through Farmingdale's electronic application system will be accepted. Once you successfully apply you will receive an email as confirmation. Returning applicants may login to their Farmingdale State College Careers Account to apply for this position. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2350 Broadhollow Road Farmingdale, NY 11735-1021"
    },
    "https://farmingdale.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=196733": {
      "title": "PRODiG+ Fellow - Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Farmingdale State College\nJob Posting: PRODiG+ Fellow - Criminal Justice Farmingdale State College \n\tJob Posting: PRODiG+ Fellow - Criminal Justice Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details PRODiG+ Fellow - Criminal Justice Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Center for Criminal Justice Studies Locations: Farmingdale, NY Posted: Jan 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Ref. No.: 26-17 Position ID: 196733 Share About Farmingdale State College: Farmingdale State College is a recognized leader in applied learning. With over 10,000 students, FSC is the State University of New York's largest college of applied science and technology, with 96% of graduates working in New York State and 75% working on Long Island. Farmingdale prepares emerging leaders in the growing technology, engineering, business and health care fields. Farmingdale State College is committed to inclusivity and excellence as part of our mission and culture. The College has received the 2022, 2023 and 2024 Higher Education Excellence in Diversity (HEED) Award. We seek candidates of all backgrounds who embrace these values and the broader mission of public higher education. The College is increasingly focused on expanding student engagement. In addition to the highly successful NCAA Division III athletic program, Esports, and an extensive array of student clubs and organizations give FSC a strong culture of civic responsibility. Job Description: Farmingdale State College invites applications for the P romoting R ecruitment, O pportunity, D iversity, I nclusion and G rowth plus ( PRODiG+ ) Post-doctoral Fellow position in the Center for Criminal Justice Studies. PRODiG+ is designed to (1) increase the number and share of excellent diverse faculty committed to advancing the ideals of diversity, equity, and inclusion; and (2) strengthening the pipeline for retention and support of these candidates.  Additional information on the PRODiG+ Fellowship can be found here . The fellowship is further designed to provide post-doctoral students interested in an academic career with a mentored experience within the academic area of Criminal Justice. Over the course of the two-year fellowship, the fellow will be engaged in teaching to include a combination of lower division and/or upper division courses in the areas of criminal justice technologies (e.g., Artificial Intelligence (AI), crime/intelligence analysis, crime mapping, forensic/crime scene), with an expected teaching load of two courses per semester. In addition, the position will expose the fellow to departmental committee work, student advisement, and/or curriculum development. The successful candidate is encouraged to engage in scholarly research and apply for relevant grants. This position will provide the fellow with direct mentorship from a faculty member within the Center for Criminal Justice Studies, as well as available campus-wide mentorship opportunities. Requirements: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: To participate in PRODiG+, candidates are required to: Be eligible to work in the United States without a visa sponsorship. Have a PhD or Terminal Degree in a field related to Criminal Justice from an accredited institution completed prior to start date. Demonstrate personal, academic, and/or work experience engaging with diversity, equity, and inclusion and/or a commitment to facilitating and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Such experience may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/ unpaid/community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations. Ability to relate to and work with students in various aspects of their academic pursuits. Excellent written and oral communications skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Preference will be given to candidates who are: Current SUNY students, alumni, and/or Fellows from a low-income background (e.g., Pell-eligible as undergraduates), were first-generation college students (students whose parents have not earned a bachelor's degree), have overcome adversity, are AmeriCorps alumni, or are veterans. Specialized in the area of technology use and application within the criminal justice domain (specifically Artificial Intelligence (AI), crime/intelligence analysis, crime mapping, forensic/crime scene, and/or related technologies) The PRODiG+ Fellowship is open to any and all prospective candidates regardless of race, color, national origin, or sex, and is consistent with all current governing federal and state nondiscrimination law. All application submissions will be assessed and evaluated in accordance with the required eligibility criteria. Additional Information: This is a 12-month Temporary position. CLOSING DATE FOR RECEIPT OF APPLICATIONS: Open Until Filled SALARY: $65,000 + $4,000 in downstate location pay = $69,000 Total Compensation. ANTICIPATED START DATE: Spring Semester 2027 The State University of New York offers excellent fringe benefits including health insurance options and retirement plans. Click here for New York State Benefits Summary Visit our Why Work at FSC page to learn more about FSC and the total rewards we offer. VISA SPONSORSHIP IS NOT AVAILABLE FOR THIS POSITION The Consumer Information web page can be viewed at the following link http://www.farmingdale.edu/consumer-information/index.shtml This page describes various services, information and statistics on many different aspects of the College's operations. Farmingdale State College's commitment to inclusive excellence is an important part of our mission of public education and our culture. At Farmingdale State College, we continue to work on building a community that supports freedom, mutual respect, and civility. We seek others who support these values of diversity and inclusiveness and candidates of all diverse backgrounds who wish to participate in our cultural aspirations are welcome and encouraged to apply. The College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status or any other legally protected status. Application Instructions: Interested candidates may apply by clicking on the \"Apply Now\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The following documents are required for all positions: Cover Letter Resume/C.V. Essay: All applicants must submit an essay, in 750 words or less, in response to the following essay prompt: \"Please describe how you've engaged, facilitated, and/or enhanced diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Examples could include personal, academic, and/or work experience and may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/unpaid/community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations.\" Additional instructions for faculty positions: Your cover letter must include a statement on teaching philosophy and methodology. Please attach copies of teaching evaluations and an unofficial copy of graduate transcripts (showing highest degree awarded/currently in process). Candidates invited for interviews will be asked to make a presentation on their research/creative activities as well as a separate teaching demonstration. Only applications made through Farmingdale's electronic application system will be accepted. Once you successfully apply you will receive an email as confirmation. Returning applicants may login to their Farmingdale State College Careers Account to apply for this position. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2350 Broadhollow Road Farmingdale, NY 11735-1021"
    },
    "https://farmingdale.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205945": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Farmingdale State College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering Technology Farmingdale State College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering Technology Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering Technology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Electrical Engineering Technology Locations: Farmingdale, NY Posted: Oct 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 27-03 Position ID: 205945 Share About Farmingdale State College: Farmingdale State College (FSC), the largest college of applied science and technology within the State University of New York system, is recognized for its applied learning. It enrolls over 10,000 students and offers nearly 50 degree programs through four schools: Arts and Sciences, Business, the Pasternack School of Engineering Technology, and the Santmann School of Health Sciences. The college's diverse offerings include the region's largest collegiate flight school, the only four-year dental hygiene program in the area, a nursing program with a 100% NCLEX pass rate, and a graduate portfolio aligned with regional needs. Master's degrees include construction management, nursing administration, and quality assurance and regulatory affairs, with additional programs in development. This is a college on the move. Construction is underway on a $75 million, 52,000-square-foot Computer Sciences Center, the first zero-net-carbon-ready building on campus, designed for our growing computing programs. Our corporate partners, including PSEG Long Island and Estée Lauder, provide scholarship funds, training programs, internships, and insight into the skills our students need to succeed.  The college's regional economic impact in 2025 was $272 million, according to an analysis conducted by the LIA Research. Faculty at FSC combine excellent teaching with active scholarship that involves undergraduates. The College has one of the most diverse student populations in the SUNY system and is federally recognized as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution. In 2026, FSC received the Higher Education Excellence and Distinction (HEED) Award from INSIGHT Into Academia. It ranks in the top 1% of colleges nationwide on the Social Mobility Index. We invite candidates from all backgrounds who are energized by the mission of public higher education and by the students it serves. Our 380-acre campus sits in the center of Long Island, roughly 35 miles from New York City, surrounded by a dense corridor of aerospace, health care, and technology employers, with beaches and parkland minutes away. Students connect through NCAA Division III athletics and an extensive array of clubs and organizations, and FSC has a strong culture of civic responsibility. If you want your teaching and scholarship to impact students' careers and a region's economy, FSC is the place. Job Description: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Technology at Farmingdale State College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Electrical and Computer Engineering Technology, beginning in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in teaching, with the ability to develop and deliver courses across the full spectrum of Electrical and Computer Engineering Technology. Teaching responsibilities will be primarily at the undergraduate level, with the potential to include graduate level courses. The department offers multiple areas of specialization, including Radio Frequency (RF) Technology. Faculty with expertise in RF and microwave systems will have access to a newly established RF/Microwave laboratory featuring state-of-the-art equipment, including C-Band and Ka-Band network analyzers, power meters, and spectrum analyzers, supporting both innovative instruction and applied research opportunities. All faculty members at Farmingdale State College have three workload components: teaching, research and scholarly activity, and service.  Candidates should have a research agenda that complements their area of academic specialty resulting in peer-reviewed publications, which are necessary for promotion and tenure at Farmingdale State College.  We are also interested in candidates with a history of, or interest in, pursuing external funding for their research.  The successful candidate will demonstrate an interest and high level of competence in teaching.  The service component of the workload includes student advising and participation on committees. Candidates must possess outstanding written and oral communication skills, and must be committed to the continuous improvement process and outcome-based assessment of the Electrical and Computer Engineering Technology programs to maintain ABET accreditation. Teaching assignments may include both day and evening classes, as well as possible online and/or hybrid course engagement. The college particularly welcomes candidates with knowledge, skills and abilities that include: Commitment to diversity and university initiatives supportive of diversity and inclusion. Interest in participating in student-centered service activities. Desire to apply expertise in promoting civic engagement with the College's many community partners. Requirements: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: An earned Doctorate in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered, provided the doctorate is conferred by the time of appointment. Demonstrated ability to conduct scholarship in Electrical or Computer Engineering or a closely related field. Excellent communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Industrial or academic experience in Electrical/Computer Engineering or a related field. College level teaching experience in Electrical/Computer Engineering, Electrical/Computer Engineering Technology, or a related field. Prior experience in course and/or program development Additional Information: This is a 10-month UUP faculty position. For the first 10 working days, beginning Tuesday, October 20, 2026 , and ending Monday, November 2, 2026 , applications will be limited to UUP Farmingdale. CLOSING DATE FOR RECEIPT OF APPLICATIONS: Open Until Filled, with priority consideration given to applications received by Wednesday, November 18, 2026. SALARY: $85,000 + $4,150 in downstate location pay = $89,150 Total Compensation. Salary may increase commensurate with qualifications and experience. ANTICIPATED START DATE: Fall semester 2027 The State University of New York offers excellent fringe benefits including health insurance options and retirement plans. Click here for New York State Benefits Summary Visit our Why Work at FSC page to learn more about FSC and the total rewards we offer. The Consumer Information web page can be viewed at the following link http://www.farmingdale.edu/consumer-information/index.shtml This page describes various services, information and statistics on many different aspects of the College's operations. Farmingdale State College's commitment to inclusive excellence is an important part of our mission of public education and our culture. At Farmingdale State College, we continue to work on building a community that supports freedom, mutual respect, and civility. We seek others who support these values of diversity and inclusiveness and candidates of all diverse backgrounds who wish to participate in our cultural aspirations are welcome and encouraged to apply. The College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status or any other legally protected status. Application Instructions: Interested candidates may apply by clicking on the \"Apply Now\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The following documents are required for all positions: Cover Letter Resume/C.V. Additional instructions for faculty positions: Your cover letter must include a statement on teaching philosophy and methodology. Please attach copies of teaching evaluations. Candidates invited for interviews will be asked to make a presentation on their research/creative activities as well as a separate teaching demonstration. Only applications made through Farmingdale's electronic application system will be accepted. Once you successfully apply you will receive an email as confirmation. Returning applicants may login to their Farmingdale State College Careers Account to apply for this position. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2350 Broadhollow Road Farmingdale, NY 11735-1021"
