    "https://farmingdale.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205953": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Medical Laboratory Science",
      "description": "Farmingdale State College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Medical Laboratory Science Farmingdale State College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Medical Laboratory Science Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor - Medical Laboratory Science Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Medical Laboratory Science Locations: Farmingdale, NY Posted: Oct 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 27-04 Position ID: 205953 Share About Farmingdale State College: Farmingdale State College (FSC), the largest college of applied science and technology within the State University of New York system, is recognized for its applied learning. It enrolls over 10,000 students and offers nearly 50 degree programs through four schools: Arts and Sciences, Business, the Pasternack School of Engineering Technology, and the Santmann School of Health Sciences. The college's diverse offerings include the region's largest collegiate flight school, the only four-year dental hygiene program in the area, a nursing program with a 100% NCLEX pass rate, and a graduate portfolio aligned with regional needs. Master's degrees include construction management, nursing administration, and quality assurance and regulatory affairs, with additional programs in development. This is a college on the move. Construction is underway on a $75 million, 52,000-square-foot Computer Sciences Center, the first zero-net-carbon-ready building on campus, designed for our growing computing programs. Our corporate partners, including PSEG Long Island and Estée Lauder, provide scholarship funds, training programs, internships, and insight into the skills our students need to succeed.  The college's regional economic impact in 2025 was $272 million, according to an analysis conducted by the LIA Research. Faculty at FSC combine excellent teaching with active scholarship that involves undergraduates. The College has one of the most diverse student populations in the SUNY system and is federally recognized as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution. In 2026, FSC received the Higher Education Excellence and Distinction (HEED) Award from INSIGHT Into Academia. It ranks in the top 1% of colleges nationwide on the Social Mobility Index. We invite candidates from all backgrounds who are energized by the mission of public higher education and by the students it serves. Our 380-acre campus sits in the center of Long Island, roughly 35 miles from New York City, surrounded by a dense corridor of aerospace, health care, and technology employers, with beaches and parkland minutes away. Students connect through NCAA Division III athletics and an extensive array of clubs and organizations, and FSC has a strong culture of civic responsibility. If you want your teaching and scholarship to impact students' careers and a region's economy, FSC is the place. Job Description: The Department of Medical Laboratory Science invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position.    The successful candidate will possess expertise in laboratory medicine and contribute to the education and mentorship of undergraduate students enrolled in our NAACLS-accredited, NYS Licensure qualifying Bachelor of Science degree program. Primary responsibilities include teaching assigned lecture and laboratory courses within the Medical Laboratory Science program; engaging in scholarly and service activities while supporting program accreditation and continuous quality improvement initiatives. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, student success, and interprofessional collaboration. All faculty members at Farmingdale State College have three workload components: teaching, research and scholarly activity, and service.  Candidates should have a research agenda that complements their area of academic specialty resulting in peer-reviewed publications, which are necessary for promotion and tenure at Farmingdale State College.  We are also interested in candidates with a history of, or interest in, pursuing external funding for their research.  The successful candidate will demonstrate an interest and high level of competence in teaching.  The service component of the workload includes student advising and participation on committees. Teaching assignments may include both day and evening classes, as well as possible online and/or hybrid course engagement. A Doctoral degree is required to be considered for tenure. The college particularly welcomes candidates with knowledge, skills and abilities that include: Commitment to diversity and university initiatives supportive of diversity and inclusion. Interest in participating in student-centered service activities. Desire to apply expertise in promoting civic engagement with the College's many community partners. Requirements: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: An earned Master's Degree in health science, education, or field related to laboratory medicine from a regionally accredited institution. ASCP certification as a Medical Technologist (MT) /Medical Laboratory Scientist (MLS). New York State Clinical Laboratory Technologist license. Three years of clinical laboratory experience. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: An earned Doctoral Degree in health science, education, or field related to laboratory medicine from a regionally accredited institution. Expertise as a generalist in the field of laboratory medicine, including microbiology. Experience as an instructor in a clinical laboratory setting. Academic teaching experience. Additional Information: This is a 10-month UUP faculty position. For the first 10 working days, beginning Tuesday, October 20, 2026 , and ending Monday, November 2, 2026 , applications will be limited to UUP Farmingdale. CLOSING DATE FOR RECEIPT OF APPLICATIONS: Open Until Filled, with priority consideration given to applications received by Wednesday, November 18, 2026. SALARY: $77,500 + $4,150 downstate location pay, salary may increase commensurate with experience ANTICIPATED START DATE: Fall semester 2027 The State University of New York offers excellent fringe benefits including health insurance options and retirement plans. Click here for New York State Benefits Summary Visit our Why Work at FSC page to learn more about FSC and the total rewards we offer. The Consumer Information web page can be viewed at the following link http://www.farmingdale.edu/consumer-information/index.shtml This page describes various services, information and statistics on many different aspects of the College's operations. Farmingdale State College's commitment to inclusive excellence is an important part of our mission of public education and our culture. At Farmingdale State College, we continue to work on building a community that supports freedom, mutual respect, and civility. We seek others who support these values of diversity and inclusiveness and candidates of all diverse backgrounds who wish to participate in our cultural aspirations are welcome and encouraged to apply. The College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status or any other legally protected status. Application Instructions: Interested candidates may apply by clicking on the \"Apply Now\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The following documents are required for all positions: Cover Letter Resume/C.V. Additional instructions for faculty positions: Your cover letter must include a statement on teaching philosophy and methodology. Please attach copies of teaching evaluations. Candidates invited for interviews will be asked to make a presentation on their research/creative activities as well as a separate teaching demonstration. Only applications made through Farmingdale's electronic application system will be accepted. Once you successfully apply you will receive an email as confirmation. Returning applicants may login to their Farmingdale State College Careers Account to apply for this position. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2350 Broadhollow Road Farmingdale, NY 11735-1021"
    }
  },
